      "stageRecord": "The demonstrative Diese heads a DP whose NP contains Bücher and an attributive AP headed by alten. The AP adjoins to N′, rather than serving as a complement of Bücher. The demonstrative, adjective, and noun have compatible plural inflection; alten has the weak adjective ending expected after this demonstrative. For gefallen, this analysis adopts a head-final VP with the experiencer mir in its specifier and the theme Diese alten Bücher in its complement domain. The theme is therefore initially VP-internal, not an external agent. The predicate assigns its theme and experiencer roles and licenses inherent dative on mir. Nominative licensing of the theme awaits finite clause structure. The words are represented as whole inflected terminals, without a separate derivation of their morphology.",
      "statement": "Construct the head-final predicate and its two arguments.",
