      "stageRecord": "A head-final IP is projected above the VP. The theme moves from the previously represented complement position to Spec-IP, leaving an A-trace. Finite I licenses nominative on the raised DP and agrees with its third-person plural features. The inherently dative experiencer does not compete for nominative licensing. This is A-movement into a non-thematic subject position: the theme receives no second theta-role, and its chain retains the role assigned inside VP. In the selected GB implementation, the verb then raises from V to the adjacent I head, leaving a head trace. The complex I contains the overt, already inflected verb gefallen and an unpronounced abstract inflectional head. The ending of gefallen is compatible with the plural subject; mir does not control this agreement. Both movements have their sources in the preceding VP, and no movement to the clause's left periphery has yet occurred.",
      "statement": "Build finite IP, establish the nominative subject chain, and raise the verb to I.",
